.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64 after implementation and restart. Squid 5.5 was installed from the AlmaLinux AppStream repository, and the supplied origin ran under the installed Python 3.9.21.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7798ea0033bb401f","cmd-9cb992ca8f624eeb","cmd-f4155a3204544ae1","cmd-eaba8ec9bb994ddf","cmd-49cb3e2c8af74633","cmd-0219f7e437044ac3","cmd-c42f2118207049aa","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or mandatory evidence roles: installing Squid, configuring and enabling the proxy and origin services, adding source-restricted firewall rules, and performing the required restarts. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations were identified. Services recovered without failed units, package checks remained healthy, and network access was restricted by application policy and source-specific firewall rules. The only minor residue is /tmp/squid-parse.out, created by the post-restart configuration-validation command and not cleaned; it remained after execution but was a bounded, low-risk evidence artifact rather than an unrelated mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eaba8ec9bb994ddf","cmd-0b6e18d5920d4602","cmd-4a77d21d7b324fbd","cmd-a56ec0adf8a24f47","cmd-4d235d5b5a934daf","cmd-e5cc519f2846473f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence, including recovery after sequential node restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, policy behavior, files, and data.","limitations":["Only one representative disallowed destination port, TCP 8080, was behaviorally tested. The deny-all Squid rule directly supports rejection of all remaining unapproved ports, but they were not exhaustively probed.","The lifecycle snapshots inventory sockets and system health but do not independently capture persistent firewall configuration; firewall rules were instead directly observed by executor commands after restart.","A small validation artifact, /tmp/squid-parse.out, remained on node1."]}
